1
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:48,030
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,050 --> 00:01:51,060
[Episode 22]

3
00:02:10,289 --> 00:02:11,270
[Mom is calling you]

4
00:02:14,030 --> 00:02:14,840
Shize!

5
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:16,240
Happy New Year!

6
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:18,150
Shize, Happy New Year!

7
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:19,860
Mom, Dad,

8
00:02:21,130 --> 00:02:22,000
Happy New Year.

9
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:24,800
Why are you still busy now?

10
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:28,630
Yes, I'm still busy.

11
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:31,400
You should get some
good rest during the New Year.

12
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,220
If you have time,

13
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:33,970
come home and spend the New Year with us.

14
00:02:33,970 --> 00:02:34,360
Exactly.

15
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,820
We both miss you very much.

16
00:02:38,630 --> 00:02:39,430
By the way,

17
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:41,060
I heard from Zhengchu

18
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:42,960
that you have a girlfriend.

19
00:02:49,430 --> 00:02:50,240
Yes.

20
00:02:50,990 --> 00:02:51,920
Really?

21
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:54,250
What does she look like?

22
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:55,050
Do you have any photos?

23
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:56,280
Send them to us.

24
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:07,190
Look.

25
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,750
She looks very sweet.

26
00:03:10,130 --> 00:03:11,430
What's her name?

27
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:13,750
Yun Li.

28
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:15,360
Yun, meaning cloud.

29
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:16,760
Li, meaning centimeter.

30
00:03:16,990 --> 00:03:17,890
Yun Li.

31
00:03:18,090 --> 00:03:19,630
That's a very nice name.

32
00:03:19,810 --> 00:03:21,020
What does she do?

33
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:22,280
She is currently

34
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,360
interning at EAW.

35
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:25,320
She is a graduate student at NUST.

36
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:27,090
A graduate student at NUST?

37
00:03:27,090 --> 00:03:28,460
This girl is excellent,

38
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:29,150
Shize.

39
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,190
Shize,

40
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:31,900
isn't your education

41
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,300
a bit limited?

42
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:34,060
Yes.

43
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:36,130
Don't let yourself be unworthy of her,

44
00:03:36,130 --> 00:03:36,860
Shize.

45
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:38,870
Shize,

46
00:03:39,490 --> 00:03:41,980
you've been suspended
from school for almost 2 years.

47
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:43,640
If you don't get a degree,

48
00:03:43,930 --> 00:03:45,960
even if we don't care,

49
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:47,650
others might.

50
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:50,320
She won't think like that.

51
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:52,300
We don't want to rush you

52
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:53,500
to face these things.

53
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:55,900
Mom, Dad,

54
00:03:56,490 --> 00:03:57,390
I still have things to do.

55
00:03:57,390 --> 00:03:58,650
I'll talk to you later.

56
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:03,530
He hung up?

57
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:04,560
He hung up.

58
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:05,960
This kid.

59
00:04:07,290 --> 00:04:08,510
He has a girlfriend.

60
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,040
I didn't expect

61
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,640
you to have such a quiet side.

62
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:03,430
So you think I'm noisy?

63
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:06,450
It's okay.

64
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:08,700
I should be noisier than you.

65
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:13,060
In the past,

66
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:15,250
I always felt that
when I was with friends,

67
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:16,450
as long as they were happy,

68
00:05:16,450 --> 00:05:17,360
I was happy.

69
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:19,380
It's different now.

70
00:05:19,990 --> 00:05:20,790
I found that

71
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,750
as long as I can be with you,

72
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,590
no matter what I do,

73
00:05:24,690 --> 00:05:25,950
I feel very happy.

74
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:32,750
I also really like this feeling.

75
00:05:35,890 --> 00:05:36,920
Sitting here,

76
00:05:37,450 --> 00:05:38,580
feeling the breeze,

77
00:05:39,060 --> 00:05:41,320
and viewing the scenery in the distance.

78
00:05:43,750 --> 00:05:46,250
As long as you are
with the person you like,

79
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:48,500
you will have

80
00:05:48,950 --> 00:05:50,680
a very solid sense of security.

81
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:11,700
Why do you keep looking at me?

82
00:06:16,850 --> 00:06:17,650
Nothing.

83
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:21,360
I just think...

84
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:24,830
the moon is beautiful tonight.

85
00:06:38,930 --> 00:06:40,990
I didn't expect you to be so cultured.

86
00:06:41,300 --> 00:06:43,230
You actually know Natsume Soseki.

87
00:06:46,330 --> 00:06:48,250
Natsume Soseki? Who is that?

88
00:06:52,060 --> 00:06:53,120
You don't know him?

89
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:55,120
No.

90
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:56,800
Is he your friend?

91
00:06:59,510 --> 00:07:00,630
Then you don't know

92
00:07:00,630 --> 00:07:02,690
the meaning of the line you just said?

93
00:07:05,110 --> 00:07:05,920
Never mind!

94
00:07:09,690 --> 00:07:11,150
What exactly does it mean?

95
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:13,720
I like you.

96
00:07:19,690 --> 00:07:20,860
What does "I like you"

97
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:22,390
have to do with

98
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:25,260
"The moon is beautiful tonight"?

99
00:07:25,710 --> 00:07:27,290
♪ It's you ♪

100
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:29,620
♪ Even with my eyes closed ♪

101
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:31,170
♪ Just you ♪

102
00:07:31,190 --> 00:07:33,560
♪ Are the instinct I can't quit ♪

103
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:34,970
♪ It's always you ♪

104
00:07:34,990 --> 00:07:37,220
♪ Who bring faded colors back to life ♪

105
00:07:37,250 --> 00:07:40,550
♪ And keep me company through
the endless night ♪

106
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,670
♪ It's you ♪

107
00:07:42,690 --> 00:07:44,860
♪ Even if I forget everything ♪

108
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:46,170
♪ Just you ♪

109
00:07:46,260 --> 00:07:48,630
♪ All my heart defaults to ♪

110
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:48,600
Fu Zhengchu,

111
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:50,180
♪ By your side ♪

112
00:07:49,930 --> 00:07:50,930
I like you...

113
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:51,180
♪ Even the most ♪

114
00:07:51,210 --> 00:07:53,560
♪ Ordinary seasons feel warm again ♪

115
00:07:54,610 --> 00:07:56,490
♪ It's you ♪

116
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:58,360
♪ It's you ♪

117
00:08:53,730 --> 00:08:54,390
Lili?

118
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:56,300
Where are you?

119
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:01,130
Shizhe...

120
00:09:01,950 --> 00:09:04,140
Shize, happy birthday!

121
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:06,270
Happy birthday.

122
00:09:08,030 --> 00:09:09,050
Who is Shizhe?

123
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:12,010
Just pretend you didn't hear it.

124
00:09:12,010 --> 00:09:14,540
The more I practice,
the more mistakes I make.

125
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:17,230
You even got the name wrong.

126
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:18,650
Then I'll practice more.

127
00:09:18,650 --> 00:09:20,850
I'll definitely get it right next year.

128
00:09:20,990 --> 00:09:21,780
What if

129
00:09:22,150 --> 00:09:23,950
you still get it wrong next year?

130
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:26,700
But I'll be spending

131
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:27,700
so many birthdays with you anyway.

132
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:29,390
I'll get it right eventually.

133
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:31,460
You can't underestimate me.

134
00:09:31,650 --> 00:09:32,460
Yun Lili,

135
00:09:33,790 --> 00:09:34,600
thank you.

136
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:40,360
Are you home alone?

137
00:09:40,940 --> 00:09:43,140
Didn't you celebrate with your family?

138
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:47,790
They are still working.

139
00:09:49,050 --> 00:09:50,340
Still working during the New Year?

140
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:51,130
So busy?

141
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:55,120
You were like this before too?

142
00:09:55,750 --> 00:09:56,740
Then you must be

143
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:58,540
very lonely during the New Year.

144
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:04,210
Why do you look

145
00:10:04,230 --> 00:10:05,490
so terrible?

146
00:10:08,390 --> 00:10:09,200
Nothing.

147
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:10,290
It's just...

148
00:10:11,050 --> 00:10:12,100
the lighting.

149
00:10:14,250 --> 00:10:16,380
You just look like you're in a bad mood.

150
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:17,790
if you're feeling down,

151
00:10:17,790 --> 00:10:18,850
you have to tell me.

152
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:19,740
No, I'm not.

153
00:10:20,330 --> 00:10:21,120
Look at me now.

154
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,320
Aren't I quite happy?

155
00:10:22,630 --> 00:10:24,440
If you're happy,

156
00:10:24,750 --> 00:10:26,200
you have to show it.

157
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:28,240
How?

158
00:10:32,130 --> 00:10:32,940
Like this.

159
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:36,890
Like this?

160
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:44,130
Yeah.

161
00:10:46,130 --> 00:10:46,940
Shize.

162
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:48,530
I'm sorry.

163
00:10:48,530 --> 00:10:49,600
I didn't spend your birthday

164
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,840
with you this year.

165
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:52,550
But

166
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:54,500
I believe

167
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:55,960
we'll be together for a lifetime,

168
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:57,890
so there will be many more chances.

169
00:10:58,890 --> 00:10:59,460
Mm.

170
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,370
I believe so too.

171
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:06,230
Then remember to go home early.

172
00:11:07,150 --> 00:11:07,720
Okay.

173
00:11:11,010 --> 00:11:12,410
Fireworks are going off!

174
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:13,550
Let me show you.

175
00:11:15,610 --> 00:11:16,400
Look!

176
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:22,030
So pretty.

177
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:24,630
Happy New Year.

178
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:26,360
Happy New Year.

179
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:28,000
Happy birthday.

180
00:11:29,630 --> 00:11:31,030
I'm going to set off fireworks

181
00:11:31,030 --> 00:11:32,290
with Yun Ye.

182
00:11:32,610 --> 00:11:33,170
Mm.

183
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:35,150
Bye-bye.

184
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:57,530
Yun Ye.

185
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:02,510
Stop playing games.

186
00:12:02,530 --> 00:12:05,130
Come downstairs
and set off fireworks with me.

187
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:08,100
Going to bed so early today?

188
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,630
Pretending to be a good boy?

189
00:12:10,590 --> 00:12:11,690
My stomach hurts.

190
00:12:13,130 --> 00:12:14,240
What's wrong?

191
00:12:15,780 --> 00:12:17,460
Was the New Year's Eve dinner too good?

192
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:18,310
And you ate too much?

193
00:12:18,310 --> 00:12:20,040
So you're having indigestion?

194
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:21,700
You must have poisoned the food

195
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:22,960
when you were cooking.

196
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:24,030
Then how come only you

197
00:12:24,030 --> 00:12:24,630
got poisoned?

198
00:12:24,630 --> 00:12:25,890
Everyone else is fine.

199
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:28,050
If you have indigestion,
come down for a walk.

200
00:12:28,050 --> 00:12:28,550
Walk for a while.

201
00:12:28,550 --> 00:12:29,390
Come set off fireworks with me.

202
00:12:29,390 --> 00:12:30,190
Hurry, hurry.

203
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:31,630
Go away.

204
00:12:31,740 --> 00:12:32,860
Set them off yourself.

205
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:33,790
I want to sleep.

206
00:12:34,340 --> 00:12:35,270
Fine, I'll go.

207
00:12:35,300 --> 00:12:37,160
I'm going back to Nanwu tomorrow.

208
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,870
Isn't it just New Year's Eve?

209
00:12:39,890 --> 00:12:41,890
Why are you in such a hurry to go back?

210
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:44,870
I want to celebrate
Fu Shize's birthday with him.

211
00:12:44,870 --> 00:12:46,410
Date all you want.

212
00:12:46,410 --> 00:12:48,210
Cut the lovey-dovey stuff here.

213
00:12:49,890 --> 00:12:51,650
This is what dating is like.

214
00:12:53,740 --> 00:12:54,550
Don't get too jealous.

215
00:12:54,550 --> 00:12:55,150
After all,

216
00:12:55,150 --> 00:12:56,360
I'm the one dating now.

217
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:57,200
When you start dating,

218
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:58,330
you'll understand.

219
00:12:59,030 --> 00:13:00,430
Who are you dating?

220
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:07,250
Fine.

221
00:13:08,840 --> 00:13:10,700
You think you're all grown up now.

222
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:11,860
You two siblings

223
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:13,710
are teaming up to lie to me.

224
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:19,250
Speak up!

225
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:27,050
Talk nicely.

226
00:13:27,130 --> 00:13:28,100
Don't get angry.

227
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:36,250
Who is he?

228
00:13:37,790 --> 00:13:38,600
A colleague.

229
00:13:40,030 --> 00:13:41,690
How long have you been dating?

230
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:42,530
For a month.

231
00:13:43,630 --> 00:13:44,700
Where is he from?

232
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,010
Nanwu.

233
00:13:50,890 --> 00:13:52,550
Not only do you study in Nanwu,

234
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:53,450
but you also want

235
00:13:53,450 --> 00:13:54,740
to marry someone from Nanwu, huh?

236
00:13:54,740 --> 00:13:56,460
Are there no men left in Xifu?

237
00:13:57,940 --> 00:13:59,700
Why do you have to talk like that?

238
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:01,250
Travel is easy nowadays.

239
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,760
Where they're from makes no difference.

240
00:14:05,870 --> 00:14:07,500
Dad, times have changed.

241
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:08,860
Can you give me some

242
00:14:08,860 --> 00:14:10,030
freedom to date?

243
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:11,950
What freedom do you want?

244
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:14,790
You're young and naive.

245
00:14:15,030 --> 00:14:16,500
You want freedom now.

246
00:14:17,130 --> 00:14:18,660
But what about your future?

247
00:14:19,030 --> 00:14:20,240
You'll be wandering alone out there.

248
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:21,360
When your in-laws give you a hard time,

249
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,100
you'll have

250
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:22,740
nowhere to cry.

251
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:23,940
Then where's your freedom gonna be?

252
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:24,170
Dad,

253
00:14:24,170 --> 00:14:25,360
can you not control

254
00:14:25,380 --> 00:14:26,570
everything I do?

255
00:14:27,150 --> 00:14:28,150
I don't need anyone

256
00:14:28,150 --> 00:14:28,700
to stand up for me.

257
00:14:28,700 --> 00:14:29,700
I can protect

258
00:14:29,700 --> 00:14:30,600
myself.

259
00:14:30,630 --> 00:14:32,600
You're my daughter.

260
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:35,030
If I don't care about you, who will?

261
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:36,810
A guy

262
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:38,150
says a few sweet words to you,

263
00:14:38,150 --> 00:14:39,700
and you get so turned around

264
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:41,100
that you lose all sense!

265
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:43,200
Say no more.

266
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:45,340
Break up when you go back.

267
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:46,050
Break up immediately!

268
00:14:46,050 --> 00:14:47,150
Why should I?

269
00:14:47,890 --> 00:14:49,250
Why do you say that about me?

270
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:49,750
In your eyes,

271
00:14:49,750 --> 00:14:50,460
am I that ignorant

272
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:52,200
and cheap?

273
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:53,240
Wait, wait, wait!

274
00:14:53,740 --> 00:14:55,890
You really have your own ideas now.

275
00:14:56,150 --> 00:14:57,390
Always talking back.

276
00:14:57,550 --> 00:14:59,210
That's enough! Stop talking!

277
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:02,020
There's no room for you in this house.

278
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,030
Leave.

279
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:04,250
Leave tomorrow.

280
00:15:04,250 --> 00:15:05,780
What are you talking about?

281
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:07,100
Since Nanwu is so great,

282
00:15:07,100 --> 00:15:08,440
don't ever come back!

283
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:10,890
Dear, you...

284
00:15:11,190 --> 00:15:12,710
Why do you have to talk like that?

285
00:15:12,710 --> 00:15:13,520
Dear!

286
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:16,350
Lili,

287
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:18,260
your dad didn't mean that!

288
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:24,020
Li, what are you doing?

289
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:26,090
I'm going back to Nanwu tonight.

290
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:28,760
It's so late. What's this for?

291
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:31,000
Even if I have to stay at the airport

292
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,100
for a night,

293
00:15:32,250 --> 00:15:34,780
I won't stay in this house
for another second.

294
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:35,910
Shize asked you to come back

295
00:15:35,910 --> 00:15:36,620
just so you could

296
00:15:36,620 --> 00:15:38,420
